      "writtenOn": "2014-07-28T21:47:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Setting this means that the vector table in use is in RAM, which is a little less secure because a RAM exploit can overwrite the vector table. I thought about making this setting only apply to RW code, but I\u0027m not sure how to do that, and I\u0027m not convinced it really makes a difference. Potentially, an attacker could do that same thing by first writing to the SYSCFG_CFGR1 register which cannot be locked down. So, I think the only big difference is the robustness against bad coding. With this change, a bad pointer that happens to modify this memory can cause serious problems.",
